                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Short version: 65%[/h1]\nFace of Envy is a conflicting game. On one side, it has great artwork, a strong plot premise, and good hidden object scenes. On the other side, we have the lack of puzzles, the incredibly repetitive story, and too much running around.\n\n[h1]Long version:[/h1]\nEuropean Mystery 2: Face of Envy is more of a reskin of the first game than a sequel.  Our French detective returns in a case very similar to his previous one, only this time he is chasing a serial attacker in Italy as he is using magical jewellery to rob victims of their physical features.\n\nThe keyword is “chasing”; the plot is an endless cycle, where every time we enter a new area, we can see the perpetrator escape to a new portion of the map, so we spend another 5-10 minutes rounding up a key to progress.\n\nThe repetitive story accompanies solid but unremarkable gameplay. There are plenty of nice hidden object scenes but few conventional puzzles (we have the running around instead). Essentially, it mostly feels like playing the leftover ideas and scenes from Scent of Desire, with slightly different scenery.",
